# Workers Static Assets custom headers: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
# Applied to responses served from the asset store (including index.html that the Worker fetches
# through env.ASSETS for browser requests to /docs). Not applied to responses the Worker builds
# itself (/v1/*, /install.sh, /healthz, text/plain /docs): worker/http.ts sets nosniff and the referrer
# policy on all of them, and worker/reports.ts adds a sandboxing CSP and X-Frame-Options to report files.
# This file is parsed at build/preview/deploy time and is never served.
#
# CSP notes: the production build has no inline <script> (Vite emits external module scripts and
# CSS); 'unsafe-inline' in style-src covers React style attributes. font-src allows data: because
# Vite inlines font files under build.assetsInlineLimit (4 KiB) as data: URIs; the
# @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono cyrillic-ext subset (2 KB) is one of them.
# Cloudflare Web Analytics is injected on the zone: its beacon loads from static.cloudflareinsights.com
# and reports to cloudflareinsights.com. Any other zone-level script injection stays blocked.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' wss: ws: https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Vite's content-hashed bundles.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted fonts: byte-for-byte copies of the pinned @fontsource-variable 5.3.0 files (src/ds/README.md, Fonts).
# They never change in place; a new font version gets a new file name.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Twin Gap Report files copied from lab/reports by scripts/sync-reports.ts (report.json, trace.json,
# calibrated_twin.json, SVGs, index.json). Paths are stable across lab re-runs and the SPA checks each file
# against the sha256 compiled into the bundle, so a cached copy from before a deploy would fail that check:
# every use revalidates (ETag, a cheap 304 when unchanged), and src/lib/reports.ts fetches with cache: no-cache.
# Long-lived, immutable copies are served by /v1/reports/:id/files/:name?sha256=<hash>.
/data/reports/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
